    "source_file": "BenchmarkSpecDefinitions.xlsx::Workload_Definitions",
    "value": "Run gpu-bench-bert-transformers-inference.py twice with Hugging Face Transformers bert-base-uncased on synthetic token batches (yaml sequence_len/batch_size, mixed_float16), parse RESULT sequences/s, tokens/s, and p50/p95/p99 latency, and average a summary row, to measure PyTorch BERT inference. This is not TensorFlow"
  },
  {
    "field_name": "Command Methodology",
    "source_file": "BenchmarkSpecDefinitions.xlsx::Workload_Definitions",
    "value": "Run gpu-bench-bert-transformers-inference.py twice with bert-base-uncased on synthetic token batches for yaml sequence_len and batch_size. Parse sequences/s, tokens/s, and p50, p95, and p99 latency, then average a summary row. This is not TensorFlow"
  },
  {
    "field_name": "Execution Description With Parameters",
    "source_file": "BenchmarkSpecDefinitions.xlsx::Workload_Definitions",
    "value": "Runs gpu-bench-bert-transformers-inference.py with Hugging Face bert-base-uncased on synthetic token batches (PyTorch, not TensorFlow). model_name, sequence_len, batch_size, warmup_iters, num_iterations, and precision mixed_float16 / f16_r come from yaml. Collector runs the script twice (pass1/pass2/summary)"
  },
